WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.133
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.868
to "The Tonight Show."
We got a great one tonight.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.033
We got a great show tonight.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.868
Guys, it is fall
in New York City,

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.100
and temperatures this week

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.200
are expected to hit 80 degrees.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.367
So goodbye, lattes.
Hello, pumpkin-spice Slurpees.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.234
Yeah!

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.767
A lot of people are talking
about this, you guys.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.200
Mike Pence is still
on the campaign trail,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.767
and he recently held an event
at a pizzeria in Iowa,

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.100
and only 13 people showed up.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.601
Can we see a photo? Ooh. Yeah.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.734
It...

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.901
It's never a good sign
when all of your followers

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.100
can be fed by two pizzas,
you know?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.934
You know you had a bad showing
when you were drowned out

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:49.167
by the sound of someone
deep-frying garlic knots.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.934
You can tell the campaign
isn't going well

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.434
because Pence also grabbed
a job application.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.501
Yeah.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.167
While he was there,
Pence ordered his favorite
pizza slice --

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.601
a plain pie
without sauce or cheese.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.400
And Pence also spoke
to some supporters

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.100
at an Iowa drug store.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.601
Take a look at this photo.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.467
This is real sad.
I mean...

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.334
Looks like he's going after that
all-important empty-chair vote.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.067
It's just -- He was so dull
that they moved him

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.234
to the sleep-aid aisle.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:21.000
It's so sad. I mean,
look at this guy right here.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.133
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.634
He's sitting there like,

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.200
"How do I say this
in the most polite way?

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.534
I'm just here for the flu shot.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:31.334
I mean, I don't want
to insult the guy."

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:34.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.400
"I'm not here for this.
I don't want to be rude."

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.834
Also, can we zoom in
on the guy's shoes?

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.501
Look at --
Look at the guy next to him.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.167
He's like, "So you're wearing
the olive-green shoes
and black socks?

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.300
I'm gonna do olive-green socks
and black shoes.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.801
So we don't match.
I don't want to match."

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.400
Some more political news.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.901
Over the weekend, nine
Republican congressmen announced

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.868
that they are running
for Speaker of the House,

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.534
and they all released statements
saying

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.801
why they're right for the job,

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.601
but a few of the candidates
stood out to me.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.801
-Really?
-Yeah, well, first up,

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.834
Austin Scott of Georgia said...

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.033
[ Mutters ]

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.000
Tom Emmer of Minnesota said...

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.300
Pete Sessions of Texas said...

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.434
I just --
They stood out to me.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.234
-That's what he said.
-He stood out to me.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:31.367
These quotes. Yeah.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.434
And then Kevin Hern
of Oklahoma said...

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.501
-Wow!
-That's what he said.

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.367
And, finally,
Jack Bergman of Michigan said...

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.234
I don't know.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.501
Well, it's been 20 days,
and the House is still locked

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.234
in a never-ending search
for a new Speaker,

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.667
but I think there may
finally be a solution.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:02.801
Check this out.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.234
-If you're looking
for a House Speaker,

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.601
then look no further!

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:09.234
Introducing the Amazon Alexa
House Speaker.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:12.234
It can vote on bills.
-Alexa: Yay. Nay.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.934
-It can heckle the President
during the State of the Union.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.467
-Alexa:
Let's go. Brandon.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:19.434
-And it can lose its job
after just a few weeks.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.601
-Alexa:
I barely unpacked my stuff.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.267
-Yeah. That's amazing.
That's cool.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.968
[ Applause ]

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.000
Well, some business news.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.067
Tesla just issued a recall
on 55,000 vehicles

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.567
over an issue with the brakes.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.000
Yeah, an issue with the brakes.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.701
You know,
when it comes to brakes,

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:49.000
you pretty much either have them
or you don't, and...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.467
Well, listen to this.
I heard that, in Turkey,

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:54.734
Uber is now offering
hot air balloon rides.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.701
I think that's great because
every time I'm in Turkey,

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:59.834
I always have a hard time
hailing hot air balloons.

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.267
"Hey..."

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.067
[ Applause ]

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.434
I think it's gonna be fun.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:08.734
It's like, "Hey, is that --
I think I see you over there.

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:11.067
I'm just -- I'm the small dot
on the other corner.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.334
I think I..."

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.167
Some TV news.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.000
Netflix just released
the official trailer

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.734
for their upcoming reality show,
"Squid Game: The Challenge."

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.400
Critics are saying it's just
like "The Golden Bachelor"

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.467
because you spent all season
hoping your favorite character

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.000
doesn't die off.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.234
Oh. Come on. Hey!
That's not...

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.400
-Hey! Wow!

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.934
-"Oh, no! Rose!"
-"Oh, God!"

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.300
-Did you guys see this?

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.100
A wax statue of
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.968
has gone viral
because people say

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.868
it doesn't look
anything like him.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.234
I don't know. Here. Take a look.

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.300
[ Laughs ]
There it is.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.200
Well, a lot of people
have spoken out about it,

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.300
including The Rock himself.
He said...

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:55.601
Then he said...

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.434
Then this wax statue
of Prince William said...

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.300
[ Applause ]

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:17.067
Then this wax statue
of Leonardo DiCaprio said...

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.267
-Wait.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:27.300
-What?
-Oh, my God.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.334
-But then this statue of
soccer star Cristiano Ronaldo

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:31.868
spoke up and said...

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.734
Then this old statue
of Lucille Ball said...

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.734
Then this old plaque
of Elvis Presley said...

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.100
And finally this wax statue
of Pope Francis said...

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:59.501
There you go. And that's true.
That's nice that he said that.

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.200
♪ You ain't nerthin'
bert a hernderg ♪

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.767
Oh, he ain't nerthin'
bert a hernderg.

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:09.400
[ Laughs ]
Guys, this is wild.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.767
Last night,
after landing at JFK Airport,

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:15.200
a JetBlue plane tipped backward
onto a wheelie --

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.868
into a wheelie.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.567
Take a look at this thing.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.501
-Ooh.
-The pilot was like,

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:24.000
"Sit, JetBlue. Sit. Good plane."

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.601
On the bright side,
the passengers in coach

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.167
got to eat all the peanuts
that rolled down

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:30.167
from first class.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:34.167
Guys, if you saw me kind of
limping on the way out here,

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.601
I got in a bike crash yesterday.
-What?!

00:06:36.601 --> 00:06:39.400
-Or an accident.
But I'm fine. But --

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.434
It was just me.
No one else was involved, but...

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:44.901
But I was --
I was riding my bike.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.367
I went to a park
with my daughter,

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:48.467
and I go, "Let's go for
a bike ride. That'd be good."

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:51.601
I haven't ridden my bike all --
well, ever.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:54.767
So I go, "Whatever.
I can figure it out. It's easy."

00:06:54.767 --> 00:06:58.133
And so I kind of got cocky
and I go, "Well, you know what?

00:06:58.133 --> 00:07:01.133
Maybe I'll just videotape
Winnie because it's cute."

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:03.067
-Yeah.
-I just want to -- For memories,

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:06.000
just to watch her on a bike
and Dad and his daughter.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.634
And so, first of all,
that's a mistake.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:10.100
-Yeah.
-You're taking the risk.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.167
-Yeah.
-One-handed.

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:12.734
-As soon as you
pull out that phone.

00:07:12.734 --> 00:07:15.234
-Yeah. So I go,
"Well, this should be good."

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.367
And then I started
picking up speed.

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:20.400
I go, "This is getting nasty."

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.968
And I go -- Well, normally
I would use this brake

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.467
because that's the back wheel.
-Right.

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:26.367
-And if you do this one,
you'll flip forward.

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:28.701
-Yeah.
-So I don't know what to do.

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:30.300
I could toss the phone.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.934
Which I should have done.
-Right.

00:07:33.934 --> 00:07:35.334
Or put it in your pocket.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:38.968
-I could have put it
in my pocket, yeah.

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.300
I got to go biking with you.
Yeah. No.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:46.234
I go -- Well, I'll just do it
but softly pull the thing.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:47.467
So I go...

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.868
So I go to do it softly.
I'm not kidding.

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:53.033
The handlebar --
The left grip handle --

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.367
I don't even know
what you call this thing.

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:58.501
Comes off.
-In your hand?

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:02.734
-Spins like it's made
out of clay or something.

00:08:02.734 --> 00:08:05.167
Bends like I'm Superman
or something.

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:08.567
I'm doing the thing, I spin it,
I flip the bike over.

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:11.501
And I just go,
"I'm okay, I'm okay."

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:14.033
Winnie kept going.
She didn't see Dad...

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:15.234
-She -- Yeah.

00:08:15.234 --> 00:08:16.467
-And she was like,
"What happened?"

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.868
I go, "Oh, my gosh, dude."
I'm totally beat up.

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:20.868
I'm scraped.
There's blood everywhere.

00:08:20.868 --> 00:08:22.634
You know what's even sadder?
-What?

00:08:22.634 --> 00:08:25.167
-Oh, it's so sad. I thought
it'd be cute if I had, like,

00:08:25.167 --> 00:08:27.167
a little, like,
a treat or something.

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:28.534
Me and Winnie
could go stop somewhere.

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:31.334
I put -- I had two apples
in a fanny pack.

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.701
It was just applesauce
by the time...

00:08:36.701 --> 00:08:38.868
[ Sad tuba plays ]
The accident.

00:08:38.868 --> 00:08:41.234
The crime scene was just
applesauce everywhere and me.

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:42.834
-Do you have footage of it?

00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:44.267
[ Drum roll ]

00:08:44.267 --> 00:08:46.334
-So I go --
She goes, "What happened?"

00:08:46.334 --> 00:08:48.367
I go, "Let's check the tape."

00:08:48.367 --> 00:08:52.067
I actually have it.
It's fine, but it's pretty --

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:53.801
It's just more sad
than anything.

00:08:53.801 --> 00:08:56.968
-Lucky you didn't have, like,
Swarovski crystals
in your pocket.

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:59.400
-No, I didn't.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.267
I don't -- I don't go bike
riding with Swarovski crystals.

00:09:02.267 --> 00:09:03.601
-You never know.

00:09:03.601 --> 00:09:05.467
-Yeah. Okay.
I guess you're right.

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:07.400
But just --
Anyways, here it is.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.934
Do I need volume?
Probably not. Anyway...

00:09:10.934 --> 00:09:12.033
Can you see it?

00:09:13.868 --> 00:09:16.300
Sorry.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.767
So now I start picking up speed.

00:09:18.767 --> 00:09:21.000
Right around here, I go,
"Oh, I got to hit the brake.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.734
I got to hit the..."
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:24.934
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

00:09:24.934 --> 00:09:26.868
[ Applause ]

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:29.534
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:33.167
-Oh, my Lord!

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:34.934
-Whew.
-Wow!

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:37.801
-Flipped. FFTEW! Yeah.

00:09:37.801 --> 00:09:39.267
-How much road rash do you get?

00:09:39.267 --> 00:09:41.367
-It's --
All my tattoos are gone.

00:09:41.367 --> 00:09:44.133
-Are you serious?!

00:09:44.133 --> 00:09:46.434
-Anyways, I'm fine.
And I'm just saying --

00:09:46.434 --> 00:09:48.601
Here's the silver lining.
Don't --

00:09:48.601 --> 00:09:50.067
The point of the thing.

00:09:50.067 --> 00:09:52.267
Don't ever videotape while
you -- You take that risk.

00:09:52.267 --> 00:09:55.534
Don't ever do that.
Yeah, but the other point?

00:09:55.534 --> 00:09:57.701
Get back on that bike.
-Yeah!

00:09:57.701 --> 00:10:00.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:03.300
-And wave all the way home!

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.968
You can go down,
but you got to get back up!

00:10:05.968 --> 00:10:08.534
Guys, it's time
for our latest installment

00:10:08.534 --> 00:10:12.033
of "Tonight Show" polls.
Here we go.

00:10:12.033 --> 00:10:14.934
-♪ "Tonight Show" polls ♪

00:10:14.934 --> 00:10:16.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:18.934
I love -- I love these --
I love these

00:10:18.934 --> 00:10:21.667
